{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And on the seventh day Elohim finished.</b> At the beginning of the seventh day — the indivisible instant which is the start of the time yet to come and is not part of it, as the Sages, of blessed memory, said (Genesis Rabbah 10:9): He entered it by a hair's breadth." "<b>And He rested on the seventh day.</b> All that day was distinguished from the first six days in the matter of cessation."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:37.698857164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}